# The claim returns the readable head - the end of the durable contiguous
# prefix - instead of the allocator head. A stale duplicate's append allocated
# but not yet durable sits above it, so the newer activation arms without
# reading it.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestClaimReadableHead
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim returns the shard's readable head, not its allocator's next offset
PERTURBS: Claim

--- FIND
        /\ claimHead' = [claimHead EXCEPT ![a] = next]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the readable head.
        /\ claimHead' = [claimHead EXCEPT ![a] =
                IF \E o \in 0..(next - 1) : o \notin durable
                THEN Min({o \in 0..(next - 1) : o \notin durable})
                ELSE next]
--- END